# IMM is not extensible (vzhn/kater-fork#38). The read e1 is in a hole
# between e0, which it depends on by address, and the write e2. Added,
# whatever it reads, it makes e0 -ppo-> e2 ([DEP] ; addr ; po ; [W], IMM's
# deps have addr ; po?) and closes the ar cycle e10 -rfe-> e0 -ppo-> e2
# -rfe-> e4 -ppo-> e5 -FSC;hb;eco;hb;FSC-> e9 -ppo-> e10 (e5 -po-> e6 -fr->
# e8 -po-> e9). Without e1 the graph is consistent: e0 and e2 are not
# ordered. kat/imm-genmc.kat now explores IMM without the po? (its ar), which
# adds e1 consistently, and leaves IMM's ar to arFull, an extra export.
e0: T0 R(x) rlx
e1: T0 R(y) rlx
e2: T0 W(z) rlx
e3: T1 TB acq
e4: T1 R(z) rlx
e5: T1 F sc
e6: T1 R(x1) rlx
e7: T2 TB acq
e8: T2 W(x1) rlx
e9: T2 F sc
e10: T2 W(x) rlx
rf: e10->e0 e2->e4
mo(x): e10
mo(z): e2
mo(x1): e8
addr: e0->e1
